  "title": "Network of autoscopic hallucinations elicited by intracerebral stimulation of periventricular nodular heterotopia: SEEG during 43 Hz and single-pulse stimulation (1 patient)",
  "description": "Stereo-EEG recordings from a single drug-resistant epilepsy patient with a right posterior temporal periventricular nodular heterotopia (PVNH). High-frequency (43 Hz) stimulation of the PVNH elicited autoscopic hallucinations, and single-pulse electrical stimulation was used to map effective connectivity. The dataset supports multi-modal connectivity analysis of the network involving the PVNH, occipital and temporal neocortex, fusiform gyrus and parietal cortex.",
  "methods_description": "Recordings were acquired at 4096 Hz with a 128-channel XLTek Quantum system from 16 depth electrodes (per the released coordinate table). Bipolar stimulation of contacts D08-D09 used a Guideline 4000LP+ stimulator. High-frequency stimulation was 43.3 Hz biphasic alternating-polarity 1 ms pulses for 5 s, at 0.25-3 mA per the article (the README task section lists 0.25-0.6 mA). Single-pulse stimulation used 20 pulses per trial with a 15 s inter-stimulus interval. A defaced T1 MRI and contact coordinates are included.",
